    "service_design": {
      "summary": "A six-week, single-account (eu-west-2, two AZ) migration POC built from versioned AWS CloudFormation held in client repositories. The Linux application package keeps its identity and runs on two private Amazon EC2 nodes in an EC2 Auto Scaling group behind an internal Application Load Balancer. Approved test clients reach the load balancer over the approved source/client network connection, proposed as AWS Site-to-Site VPN. The application writes to one authoritative Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL Multi-AZ DB instance, which replicates synchronously to a standby in the second AZ. The standby is not used for reads. Media is read from a private, KMS-encrypted Amazon S3 bucket through an S3 gateway endpoint. Schema objects are pre-created with native PostgreSQL tooling from a private migration-runner EC2 instance. AWS DMS performs full load plus ordered CDC with validation. AWS DataSync copies media with verification. Reconciliation scripts write the migration ledger, exception records and delta ledger as versioned run records to an S3 evidence bucket. Cutover and rollback are human-gated runbooks; there is no orchestration product. Single-writer control uses database write grants plus an active-environment flag in Systems Manager Parameter Store that also gates the import scheduler. Post-write rollback captures target-only changes with a second DMS CDC task from RDS to S3 starting at the write-release position, so no reverse writer path is created. Recovery uses native RDS Multi-AZ failover and point-in-time restore to an isolated instance; there is no separate backup product. Operations use CloudWatch dashboards, logs and alarms routed to SNS, RDS event notifications for backup failures, CloudTrail for AWS API audit, Inspector for vulnerability findings, and Budgets plus Cost Explorer for daily cost tracking and the 70%/90% alerts, which are notifications and not hard caps. All services are proposals pending G1 approval.",
      "capabilities": [
        {
          "id": "c4",
          "name": "Application tier and ingress",
          "evidence_quote": "Amazon EC2 instances in private subnets behind an internal Application Load Balancer; approved test clients only",
